- name: note_3
  id: note
  parameters:
    alias: ''
    comment: 'This process creates a lowpass sinc curve,

      then transforms it into a highpass sinc curve

      by subtracting the lowpass impulse response

      from an all-pass impulse response.

      1) Calculate the number of required taps

      2) Calculate the sinc curve based on the

      cutoff frequency and number of taps

      3) Calculate an all-pass impulse response

      based on the number of taps.

      4) Subtract the lowpass filter impulse

      response from the all-pass impulse response

      to create the highpass impulse response.

      This is the spectral inversion method.

      5) Window and normalize the gain of the

      highpass sinc curve to make the final

      highpass filter.'
    note: Process to Create HPF
  states:
    bus_sink: false
    bus_source: false
    bus_structure: null
    coordinate: [280, 280.0]
    rotation: 0
    state: enabled
